internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1231-- **B44 remains open:** an attach receipt proves an admitted client claim, not
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1232-  a live tmux client. This protocol has no positive client identity/detach
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1233-  signal. Unknown liveness remains a possible peer and can conservatively block
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1234-  a later attach after detach. Owner: future authoritative receipt/protocol
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1235-  owner; overlap policy remains in `internal/termbind` and `executeAttach`.
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1236-- **B46:** after the second socket `lstat` confirms the same inode, a pathname
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1237-  replacement can still race before the OS `connect` resolves the pathname.
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1238-  Unix has no portable path-relative connect identity pin. Tests prove the
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1239-  injected swap during custody validation is refused before `Dial`; this
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1240-  narrower post-check interval remains owner-named and is not claimed closed.
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1241-- **Section 4.E replication:** no new replication prohibition claim is made;
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md-1242-  the runtime package has no replication transport to exercise in this leaf.
