.temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt/TASK-260830-g0pcnt_conformance-matrix.md:257:### Revision 2 — permission-bit custody census and importer outcomes
.temp/TASK-260830-g0pcnt/TASK-260830-g0pcnt_conformance-matrix.md:261:For non-Ax-owned system ancestors, SPEC §3.2 lines 810–812 requires rejecting unsafe permissions but does not prescribe a numeric mode mask. The implementation rejects group/other write because it can replace the derived socket and admits non-writable read/execute bits for path traversal. This is recorded as an interpretation, not as a numeric requirement stated by the specification. Sticky shared ancestors are separately driven at 01777 through all three entries by `TestCustodyPermissionBitCensusAdmitsStickyAncestor`.
