internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md:1244:## Permission-bit custody census — SPEC §3.2
internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md:1248:For non-Ax-owned system ancestors, SPEC §3.2 lines 810–812 requires rejecting unsafe permissions but does not prescribe a numeric mode mask. The implementation rejects group/other write because it can replace the derived socket and admits non-writable read/execute bits for path traversal. This is recorded as an interpretation, not as a numeric requirement stated by the specification. Sticky shared ancestors are separately driven at 01777 through all three entries by `TestCustodyPermissionBitCensusAdmitsStickyAncestor`.
