Axis count for this leaf: **6 of 30 cells** are directly measured by named
tests plus narrowing mutants; the other 24 cells are explicitly bounded or
unreachable above. No tmux process runs in these tests.

#### Bounds dispositioned by this leaf

- **B44 remains open:** an attach receipt proves an admitted client claim, not
  a live tmux client. This protocol has no positive client identity/detach
  signal. Unknown liveness remains a possible peer and can conservatively block
  a later attach after detach. Owner: future authoritative receipt/protocol
  owner; overlap policy remains in `internal/termbind` and `executeAttach`.
- **B46:** after the second socket `lstat` confirms the same inode, a pathname
  replacement can still race before the OS `connect` resolves the pathname.
  Unix has no portable path-relative connect identity pin. Tests prove the
  injected swap during custody validation is refused before `Dial`; this
  narrower post-check interval remains owner-named and is not claimed closed.
- **Section 4.E replication:** no new replication prohibition claim is made;
  the runtime package has no replication transport to exercise in this leaf.

## Exhaustive custody-mode oracle — pinned SPEC v0.7.0 §3.2

The oracle in TestCustodyModeOracleAtProductionEntries is independent of the
production predicates and enumerates every 12-bit Unix mode from 0000 through
07777 for each component class at Probe, Spawn, and Execute. That is 4 × 4096 ×
3 = 49,152 mode/class/entry inputs. Each of the 12 named subtests asserts that
the production decision equals the specification-derived oracle. Admitted
inputs reach the fake next-stage effect; refused inputs return the expected
literal typed refusal and produce zero Dial, spawn, or dispatch effects.

The specification says the AX-created runtime tmux directory is owned by the
current user and mode 0700, component custody does not follow symlinks, and
unsafe kind, ownership, or permissions must be refused before bind, connect,
rename, or unlink (§3.2, lines 806–813). The independent mode rules are:

| Component class | Oracle admits | Production predicate |
|---|---|---|
| Socket leaf | Owner read/write, optional owner execute toggle, no group/other bits, no special bits | ownerOnlySocketMode via checkCustodySocket |
| Runtime tmux directory | Exactly 0700 with no special bits | ownerOnlyRuntimeDirMode via commitRuntimeDir / verifyRuntimeDir |
| Runtime root | Exactly 0700 with no special bits | ownerOnlyCustodyRootMode via checkCustodyRoot |
| Ancestor | No group/other write, or sticky set; setuid and setgid never replace sticky | writableByOthers via checkCustodyAncestors |

The test projects modes at the production predicate seam while leaving fixture
objects private. The socket leaf is a synthetic socket FileInfo backed by a
regular file; fake dialers and runners observe effects. No real socket is
bound or connected, and no tmux process is started. Every input must hit the
projected production predicate or the subtest fails.

| Gate | Component class | Entry | Executed subtest | Isolated admitting narrowing killed |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| checkCustodySocket | socket_leaf | ServerProber.Probe | TestCustodyModeOracleAtProductionEntries/socket_leaf/Probe | N-socket-mask-drop-group-triplet, N-socket-mask-drop-other-triplet, six N-socket-mask-drop-* single-bit rows, N-socket-combination-admit |
| checkCustodySocket | socket_leaf | ServerSpawner.Spawn | TestCustodyModeOracleAtProductionEntries/socket_leaf/Spawn | N-socket-mask-drop-group-triplet, N-socket-mask-drop-other-triplet, six N-socket-mask-drop-* single-bit rows, N-socket-combination-admit |
| checkCustodySocket | socket_leaf | Lifecycle.Execute | TestCustodyModeOracleAtProductionEntries/socket_leaf/Execute | N-socket-mask-drop-group-triplet, N-socket-mask-drop-other-triplet, six N-socket-mask-drop-* single-bit rows, N-socket-combination-admit |
| ownerOnlyRuntimeDirMode | runtime_tmux_dir | ServerProber.Probe | TestCustodyModeOracleAtProductionEntries/runtime_tmux_dir/Probe | N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-group-triplet, N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-other-triplet, six N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-* single-bit rows, N-runtime-dir-combination-admit |
| ownerOnlyRuntimeDirMode | runtime_tmux_dir | ServerSpawner.Spawn | TestCustodyModeOracleAtProductionEntries/runtime_tmux_dir/Spawn | N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-group-triplet, N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-other-triplet, six N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-* single-bit rows, N-runtime-dir-combination-admit |
| ownerOnlyRuntimeDirMode | runtime_tmux_dir | Lifecycle.Execute | TestCustodyModeOracleAtProductionEntries/runtime_tmux_dir/Execute | N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-group-triplet, N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-other-triplet, six N-runtime-dir-mask-drop-* single-bit rows, N-runtime-dir-combination-admit |
| ownerOnlyCustodyRootMode | root | ServerProber.Probe | TestCustodyModeOracleAtProductionEntries/root/Probe | N-root-mask-drop-group-triplet, N-root-mask-drop-other-triplet, six N-root-mask-drop-* single-bit rows, N-root-admit-0750 |
